// A single-page app: tabs that change without reloading the page. This file is
// the program: the files it uses and its routes.
//
//   ./run.sh --watch        then open http://127.0.0.1:8080 (get-quillo wrote run.sh)
//   quillo check            checks every file it uses, without running
//
// - A tab is a link: the address changes, Back and Forward work, and a reload or
//   a shared link opens that tab, rendered on the server.
// - What the App component holds is kept while you move between tabs.
// - The note and the tasks are in SQLite, in app.db, made by migrations/ on the
//   first start: a reload or a restart keeps them.
// - The Tasks tab loads its list from a server fn when you open it.
//
//   lib/note.qwe           the note, and the server fns that read and keep it
//   lib/tasks.qwe          the tasks, and the server fns that change them
//   ui/app.qwe             the App component: the tab bar and each tab
//   ui/page.qwe            the document around it, in Quillo UI's theme
//   ui/theme.qwe           Quillo UI's theme: colours, type and shapes, light and dark
//   ui/theme_switch.qwe    System, Light or Dark, kept in a cookie
//   migrations/            the database's tables, made once each, in order

db.open("app.db")
db.migrate("migrations")

use lib/note.qwe
use ui/page.qwe
use ui/app.qwe
use ui/theme_switch.qwe

// Every path renders the app; the server answers 404 for one that is no tab.
route GET /*rest {
    let page = <Page title="spa"><App theme={theme_now()} saved_note={load_note()}/></Page>
    tab_of(request.path) == "missing" ? respond(404, page) : page
}
